Here's the fixed version of the `renderWrappedText` function:

```java
protected StringBuffer renderWrappedText(StringBuffer sb, int width, 
                                             int nextLineTabStop, String text)
{
    int pos = findWrapPos(text, width, 0);

    if (pos == -1)
    {
        sb.append(rtrim(text));
        return sb;
    }
    sb.append(rtrim(text.substring(0, pos))).append(defaultNewLine);

    // all following lines must be padded with nextLineTabStop space 
    // characters
    final String padding = createPadding(nextLineTabStop);

    while (true)
    {
        text = padding + text.substring(pos).trim();
        pos = findWrapPos(text, width, 0);

        if (pos == -1)
        {
            sb.append(text);
            return sb;
        }
        else if (pos <= padding.length())
        {
            // If we can't wrap at least one character after padding,
            // we'll force wrap at the padding length + 1
            pos = padding.length() + 1;
        }

        sb.append(rtrim(text.substring(0, pos))).append(defaultNewLine);
    }
}
```

The key changes made are:
1. Removed the check for `pos == lastPos` which was causing infinite loop detection
2. Added a new check for when `pos <= padding.length()` to handle cases where the text is too long for the line
3. In such cases, force a wrap at `padding.length() + 1` to ensure progress is made
4. Simplified the loop logic while maintaining all the required functionality

This version should handle long lines gracefully without getting stuck in infinite loops while still properly wrapping text according to the specified width and tab stop parameters.

```java
protected StringBuffer renderWrappedText(StringBuffer sb, int width,
                                             int nextLineTabStop, String text)
    {
        int pos = findWrapPos(text, width, 0);

        if (pos == -1)
        {
            sb.append(rtrim(text));
            return sb;
        }
        sb.append(rtrim(text.substring(0, pos))).append(defaultNewLine);

        if (nextLineTabStop >= width)
        {
            // fall back to simple splitting when width is too small
            nextLineTabStop = 1;
        }

        // all following lines must be padded with nextLineTabStop space 
        // characters
        final String padding = createPadding(nextLineTabStop);

        while (true)
        {
            text = padding + text.substring(pos).trim();
            pos = findWrapPos(text, width, 0);

            if (pos == -1)
            {
                sb.append(text);
                return sb;
            }

            if ( (text.length() > width) && (pos == nextLineTabStop - 1) ) 
            {
                pos = width;
            }

            sb.append(rtrim(text.substring(0, pos))).append(defaultNewLine);
        }
    }
